    "updated_at": "2026-11-26T06:53:58Z",
    "body": "I could not reproduce this on upstream/main e4d57ee6a. Claim released.\n\nWhat I tried:\n\n- I changed the unit of `testdata/models/box.step` to nine forms of an inch unit and imported each form through `camcraft_kernel::solidcore_step::import_step`.\n- The forms were: `CONVERSION_BASED_UNIT('inch',#n)` in lower case, a base of `.MILLI.`, `.CENTI.` (2.54) or `$` (0.0254) `.METRE.`, `MEASURE_WITH_UNIT` in place of `LENGTH_MEASURE_WITH_UNIT`, `POSITIVE_LENGTH_MEASURE`, compact and multi-line records, and a different record order.\n- Eight forms read 25.4 mm for each unit. The 1 mm cube came out 25.4 mm.\n- One form (a complex `(LENGTH_MEASURE_WITH_UNIT() MEASURE_WITH_UNIT(..))`) is refused by name: \"length unit #12 cannot be converted to millimetres\". It is not read as mm.\n- `testdata/models/Milling-test-inch.step` also imports at the correct size (`step_chord_units.rs`).\n- The app path (`ImportModel::within_in` -> `parse_with_cause_in` -> `parse_open_assuming`) uses the unit that the kernel reads. I found no second reader that ignores it.\n- No commit between 034e91b8b and e4d57ee6a changes the STEP unit path.\n\nThe bug is likely in a part of the real file that my forms do not have. Examples are a second representation context, or an assembly structure.\n\n@mike-lloyd03 can you attach the STEP file, or a small inch part from Fusion that shows the same problem? Please also send the import notes for that model (the \"length unit: ...\" line). The notes show the unit that CamCraft read.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
